menu "Updates (OTA)"

config DL_OTA_MANIFEST_URL
    string "Manifest URL"
    default "https://github.com/slastra/downlink/releases/latest/download/manifest.json"
    help
        Where boards look for new releases. GitHub redirects "latest" to the
        newest non-prerelease, so publishing a release is the whole rollout.
        Overridable per check over MQTT ({"cmd":"ota.check","manifest":...}).

config DL_OTA_CHECK_H
    int "Hours between checks"
    default 6
    range 1 168
    help
        A check only reports what is available (status "ota.available"); an
        install needs {"cmd":"ota"}. The first check is a minute after the
        broker first connects; a failed one is retried after 30 minutes.

config DL_OTA_CONFIRM_MIN
    int "Minutes for a new image to reach the broker"
    default 10
    range 1 120
    help
        A new image must reach the broker within this long after boot, or the
        board rolls back to the previous one. Reaching the broker is what
        proves it can still be managed (and updated again).

config DL_OTA_PAUSE_MS
    int "Pause after each 4 KB written (ms)"
    default 10
    range 0 200
    help
        Each flash sector erase stalls both cores and PSRAM for tens of ms.
        The music is faded out for the download (the stalls chop it up
        audibly even when the output never underruns), so this only leaves
        the other tasks (WiFi, MQTT, the player) room between erases.
        0 writes flat out.

endmenu
